//! Generated ACLE intrinsics: which each instruction realises, and where its arguments are.
//!
//! `INTRINSIC_DEFS` is every intrinsic ACLE names, once each, in name
//! order; an index into it is `Intrinsic::id`, an intrinsic's identity.
//! `INTRINSICS` is every *binding* of one to an encoding, so a name
//! appears once per encoding that realises it, and `Instruction::intrinsics`
//! returns the run belonging to the instruction. Every index in a binding,
//! `Source::Operand(1)` or `Output::Element { operand, .. }`, is an index
//! into `Instruction::operands`, not into either table. See
//! `crate::intrinsics` for what each field means.
//!
//! Auto-generated by exarmo-aarch64-gen. Do not edit manually.

